+### What the evidence establishes and what it does not
+
+Established: the readiness probe is firing persistently; the named Executive
+office agent is idle, never started and its readiness record is stale; the
+signal recurred after an earlier clearance; delegated PnP workers remain active.
+This is a genuine office-liveness observation and a limitation on Executive
+coordination at the time of review.
+
+Not established: that any specific assigned task was neglected or falsely
+reported delivered; that the Executive office is permanently incapacitated;
+that any cause, root failure or material impediment to a named board issue
+exists (the Judiciary mailbox inbox was empty — no material blocker report was
+pending); or that any test, CI job or independent check failed or was disabled.
+GitHub-hosted CI is not implicated in a readiness probe.
+
+Auto-close after 20 consecutive clear observations remains a collector rule
+(Founder directive 2026-11-16), not proof that a cause was repaired. With
+`clear_observations` at 0, this case is not close-eligible; the Judiciary did
+not close it and did not ask the Executive to repair itself.
+
+### Measurement limitation reported to Parliament (not reformed)
+
+The probe observes a readiness field and auto-clears on absence of the signal;
+it cannot distinguish a session rotation from loss of office function, cannot
+measure whether useful work was delivered, and here reports `model`/`variant`
+as `unknown`. The repeated clearance-then-re-fire sequence shows that a clear
+run is not a durable recovery. Under Act 15 §2 the design of this instrument is
+Parliament's to change, not the Judiciary's; no change is proposed or made.
